[02:23.64] Now in this far away land
[02:29.76] Strange that the palms of my hands
[02:34.62] Should be damp with expectancy
[02:38.07] 
[03:51.06] Spring, and the air's turning mild
[03:57.58] City lights and the glimpse of a child
[04:02.66] Of the alleyway infantry
[04:05.74] 
[04:10.05] Friends, do they know what I mean?
[04:16.24] Rain and the gathering green
[04:21.14] Of an afternoon out of town
[04:25.17] 
[04:29.21] But Lord I had to go
[04:32.39] The trail was laid too slow behind me
[04:38.44] To face the call of fame
[04:41.89] Or make a drunkard's name for me
[04:47.83] Though now this better life
[04:51.38] Has brought a different understanding
[04:57.51] And from these endless days
[05:01.16] Shall come a broader sympathy
[05:04.30] 
[05:07.36] And though I count the hours
[05:10.96] To be alone's no injury
[05:15.42] My home was a place by the sand
[05:23.05] Cliffs and a military band
[05:28.23] Blew an air of normality
[05:29.32] 